ith 2 cards teammate can likely play a pair or sequence if possible — though we don’t know teammate’s exact cards, the game’s dynamics suggest we want to transfer turn to teammate when they are close to going out.  \n\n**Reason:**  \n- BlackJoker cannot be beaten in single combat except by RedJoker (absent here).  \n- Forces landlord to pass, gives teammate control with 2 cards left.  \n- Even if teammate only has a pair or high cards, they can potentially finish in 2 plays.  \n- Holding BlackJoker for later is not useful if I never get another free play before landlord goes out.  \n\n**Answer:**  \n{"cards": ["BlackJoker"]}  \n\n**Final output:**  \nEvaluation: Best move is to play BlackJoker to seize control and pass turn to teammate with 2 cards left, forcing landlord to pass.  \nReason: BlackJoker is unbeatable here and maximizes chance for teammate to go out before landlord.  \nAnswer: {"cards": ["BlackJoker"]}'}
